                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.06563/2610.06563v1/co-evolution_v3.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Harness–environment co-evolution.Given an environment pool of feasible and infeasible tasks and current harness, paired rollouts and failure diagnosis are used to iteratively evolve both the environment pool and harness. Environment evolution(top)constructs, validates, and selects new feasible–infeasible task pairs to challenge the current agent and expand the training pool. Harness evolution(bottom)similarly refines the harness iteratively on the expanded task pool, with each updated harness selected from candidates using performance on a validation set.",
